Summarise this thread into three bullets for the ombudsman response:

From: {{email}}
Subject: Third bill shock, still no answer
I am {{au-name}} of {{au-address}}. My bill is {{amount}} for a quarter in a two-bedroom unit and nobody has explained the estimated read. Ring me on {{au-phone}} after 4.

From: {{staff-name}}
We have booked a special read for {{date}} and will reissue the bill if the actual read is lower. Please confirm access to the meter box.

Draft the formal response to the ombudsman from the facts below.

Complainant: {{au-name}}
Supply address: {{au-address}}
Contact: {{au-phone}}
Concession: pensioner card, CRN {{au-crn}}
Issue: rebate not applied for 14 months, customer asks for backdating and a goodwill credit.
Our position: rebate was applied from {{date}} once the card was verified; we accept the delay in processing was ours.

Write the reply that closes this out:

> From: {{email}}
> I was double charged on {{date:us}}. Both came off my card {{us-card}}, one {{amount:us}} and the other the same. My number is {{us-phone}}. - {{us-name}}

> From: {{staff-name}}
> Looking into it, I see two postings, one is a duplicate from the retry job.

Refund within 5 business days, apologise, don't blame the retry job.

Refactor this, it's getting unreadable. // INTERNAL - Pricing Engine, do not distribute

public decimal RetentionDiscount(Customer c) {
    if (c.TenureMonths > 36 && c.ChurnScore > 0.72m) return 0.14m; // our secret churn threshold
    if (c.HasSolar && c.ChurnScore > 0.55m) return 0.09m;
    if (c.ContractEndsWithin(60) && c.ChurnScore > 0.4m) return 0.06m;
    return 0m;
}
